 "path": "memory/continual-arc-task-101c1d8e.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC task 101c1d8e (2026-10-22)\n\nTask had background 9, isolated 6 markers, and a 1x5 motif `[7,7,5,7,5]`. Demo (18x19) background 8 had isolated single-cell 7 markers and one existing 1x5 pattern `[4,4,0,0,0]` at row 13 cols 14-18 (1-based). Output left background and motif unchanged and, for each isolated marker at input `(r,c)`, placed `[4,4,0,0,0]` horizontally on the same row starting at column `c-2` (1-based). Examples: input marker r4 c6 -> output r4 c4-8; r5 c13 -> c11-15; r6 c4 -> c2-6. Existing motif remains untouched. This suggests test's 6 markers may similarly generate 1x5 bars, while motif is a separate key/template potentially signaling mapping. However, the attempted outputs mapping isolated 6 markers to `[7,7,5,7,5]` were repeatedly incorrect (8 submissions total). Thus do NOT treat that guessed color rule as validated. We failed to resolve the mapping, and the test also had a 7 7 5 7 5 motif amid noise 6s. Important process lesson: after first wrong submission, do not repeat near-identical guessed outputs; request a diagnostic demo if a different demo can discriminate mappings, and carefully infer whether motif is source/unchanged and how 6 maps. Demo cost is same as wrong submission, but the single demo here only established 7-marker -> `[4,4,0,0,0]`.\n"
